From 71989984eb5381aed84a41004e88bc402533d115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:13:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Reuse validated shared-blocker inputs within a
 derivation

Reduce repeated cohort and check-event scans without caching mutable blocker decisions. Scope reuse to synchronous calls; invalidate for writes, aliases, clock and physical identity; bypass transactions and retain fresh post-command fences. RED: real due pass scanned cohort five times rather than once. GREEN: 158 focused blocker tests before two added commit/race regressions; final input file 15 passed. Synthetic input-only replay at 100/1000/5000 rows: 6.67/54.64/282.42ms baseline vs4.18/34.11/168.77ms scoped. Config mocked equally; not whole-reclaim/live proof. G2b remains incomplete pending mutation/scale review, CI, canonical ship and <=0.4% live P1.
